# Secrets (root-level only — charts/*/templates/secrets/ are Helm
# templates, not actual secrets). Use `/secrets/*` (not `/secrets/`)
# so the negation below works: gitignore docs say a re-included file
# is impossible if the parent directory itself is excluded, only if
# its CONTENTS are excluded with a glob.
/secrets/*
# DO commit `.example` template files so operators have a starting
# shape for the gitignored .txt files (ADR-048 PR-B2 added Docker Hub
# PAT templates).
!/secrets/*.example
*.pem
*.key
# Chart-vendored public trust roots are explicit exceptions —
# these are public CA certificates (no private key material).
# Backlog #13 anchor: SwissSign 2020-2 root extracted from
# `main_signed.pdf` PAdES chain.
!charts/audittrace/trust-store/static-roots/*.pem
!charts/audittrace/trust-store/static-roots/*.crt

# Docker
docker-compose.override.yml

# Testing
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.tox/

# MyPy
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# Ruff
.ruff_cache/

# ChromaDB
chroma_data/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local agent config (your IP)
.opencode/

# Project-local CLAUDE.md — personal orientation file for Claude Code sessions,
# not a shared project artefact. AGENTS.md is the shared equivalent.
/CLAUDE.md

# Personal skill library (your IP) — seeded into procedural memory at runtime,
# must not be committed. SKILL-memory-commands.md is project-local, keep it.
memory/procedural/SKILL-*.md
!memory/procedural/SKILL-memory-commands.md

# Generated artifacts
coverage.xml
junit.xml
test_data/

# Throwaway artefacts — eval JSONLs, smoke traces, ad-hoc Python probes,
# diagnostic dumps. Never committed; if something here matters it gets
# promoted to docs/ or scripts/. Listed because `git add -A` was caught
# accidentally staging these on 2026-04-26.
/tmp/

# Client keys (generated by scripts/generate-client-keys.sh)
keys/
# Structurizr local-render byproducts (the DSL is the source of truth;
# .structurizr/ is the server's working dir, workspace.json is generated).
.structurizr/
docs/architecture/workspace.json
istio-1.29.2/

# Per-deployment Helm values — holds dev secrets + the operator's
# hostname overrides (e.g. audittrace.allaboutdata.eu for Google
# federation). Each operator maintains their own; never committed.
charts/audittrace/values-local.yaml

# WS2 deploy-runner evidence bundles (deploy reports + pod samples)
scripts/deploy/runs/

# Fault-injection runner evidence bundles (sibling of runs/ above)
scripts/deploy/faultinject-runs/

# Session scratch — briefs, PR-body drafts, work-start/park memos, build
# logs, cert artefacts. Local-only working files; some reference private
# counterparty material and must NEVER reach this public repo.
scratchpad/

# #398 release-cut runner evidence bundles (release-record JSON + summary)
scripts/release/runs/

# ADR-062 Phase B WU-B6 corpus-backfill runner evidence bundles
scripts/migrate/runs/

# Local Claude Code config + agent definitions — never committed (IP: kept local, not shared).
.claude/

# PR-body content is PRIVATE — it lives in
# ~/work/audittrace-private/pr-bodies/ and is only ever pointed to via the
# PR_BODY env var (see .githooks/pre-push, #397). This repo never tracks a
# PR body; the guard below stops a stray copy from ever being staged,
# anywhere in the tree (no leading `/`, so it matches at any depth, not
# just the repo root).
#
# Matches the documented PR-body-authoring convention basename PR-BODY.md
# (feedback_gh_pr_body_from_file) PLUS any case variant / prefixed /
# suffixed shape (PR-BODY-393.md, my-PR-BODY-thing.md, pr-body.md, ...).
# A single `/PR-BODY-*.md` glob (the original, too-narrow guard) missed
# the bare `PR-BODY.md` convention name and the lowercase spelling —
# caught by review 2026-08-03; verified below with `git check-ignore -v`
# and pinned by tests/test_gitignore_pr_body_guard.py.
*PR-BODY*.md
*pr-body*.md
*.pr-body.md
